  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Finite type over a separated target",
  "statement": "In a commutative triangle $T\\to Y\\to B$, if $T\\to B$ is of finite\ntype and $Y\\to B$ is separated, then $T\\to Y$ is of finite type.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-closure/lemma-nagata-finite-type-to-separated-target.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-finite-type-to-separated-target, order 78"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Factor $T\\to Y$ as its graph\n\n$$\nT\\longrightarrow T\\times_BY\\longrightarrow Y.\n$$",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    },
    {
      "text": "The graph is a closed immersion because $Y\\to B$ is separated, hence is\nof finite type. The second map is the base change of the finite-type\nmorphism $T\\to B$. Their composite is therefore of finite type.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
